// Regression fixture: free-form prose inside @Description{...} that parses
// as a C++ declaration.
//
// The minimal leaking shape is `Word Word, Word (...)`: source.cpp reads it
// as a declaration with a comma-separated declarator list whose last
// declarator has a constructor-style initializer --
//   `A B, C (D)`  ==  type A, declarator B, declarator C(D)
// MFront prose ends sentences with '.', never ';', so that declaration is
// never terminated. Its meta.declaration.cpp scope then swallows the block's
// own closing '}' and leaks to EOF, suppressing keyword.control.mfront on
// every @keyword below.
//
// Academic citations hit this shape naturally, which is how it shows up in
// real files. The example below is the one @maxence-wz used while reviewing
// PR #1.
//
// Every line starting with @Xxx in this file must be highlighted.

@DSL Implicit;
@Behaviour DescriptionProse;

@Description
{
  Reference Smith, J. (2020). Some Journal(Volume, Issue).
};

@MaterialProperty real k;

@Epsilon 1.e-14;
@Theta 1.0;
